From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 00:03:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11145/11362] [outer-loop] Eval runs declare provenance and
 their envelope (REQ-ARC-WMTE-7021, 7022)

Operator-authorized. Two halves of one gap: an eval run could say neither what
kind of solve it was nor what hardware produced it.

7021 stamps solve_provenance: live_agent_self_discovery. The harness runs the
live agent frame-only with no GameAdapter and no banked plan, so that is true
by construction. It was previously inferred inside a single consumer, while the
second source in that same function demands the stamp and would have credited
these runs zero.

7022 records the envelope: requested context size, requested generator GPU,
CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES, server and model paths, the GPU rows the DRIVER
attributes to this process tree, resolved indices, hostname. Thirteen of
thirteen prior artifacts recorded none of it, so the n_ctx conclusion and the
engine table rested on runs that could not say what produced them. That is a
G2 gap, not a cosmetic one.

Requested and held are separate fields deliberately. On 2026-09-04 a run set
CARNOT_ARC_GENERATOR_CUDA_GPU=1 and llama.cpp still split a 27B across both
cards. An envelope recording only the request would preserve the exact
misreport it exists to prevent.

Absence is recorded rather than omitted: a missing key and a measured 'none'
are different facts, and a mutation covers it. The envelope is read once and
cached so two games in one run cannot disagree about the hardware.

It lives in its own module rather than in the eval script for two reasons: it
is producer-agnostic, and importing the eval pulls in about half a gigabyte of
the carnot stack, which the per-test memory watchdog correctly refuses. That
made the function untestable in place; extracting it was the fix, not a bypass
of the guard.

Also commits a fresh exp6968 artifact from running it to answer whether the new
evidence directories satisfy its gate. They do not: transition_source_path now
resolves to a real transitions.jsonl, but the consumer reads it with
json.loads over the whole file and JSONL is not one object, so the read returns
None and immutable_transition_source stays False. Diagnosis only; the gate is
not changed here.

5 tests, 3/3 mutations RED with byte-identical restores.

